{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs22 \li0 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs22 \li0 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs22 \sa0 \sb0 
This note provides an overview of the Uniform Customs and Practice for Documentary Credits (UCP), 2007 Revision, ICC Publication No. 600 (UCP 600) which superseded the previous edition of the UCP, UCP 500. Where relevant this note also draws comparisons between the UCP 600, the UPC 500 and the International Standby Practices, ICC Publication No. 590 (ISP 98).
\par 
}
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs22 \sa0 \sb0 
\u160\'3f
\par 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs22 \li0 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs22 \li0 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs22 \sa0 \sb0 
The UCP is a set of contractual rules which are frequently incorporated by express agreement into a documentary credit (also called a letter of credit) transaction.
\par 
}
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs22 \sa220 \sb0 
\u160\'3f\u160\'3f
\par 
}
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li0 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
\u160\'3f
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
\u160\'3f
\par 
}
{\b0 \cf31 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li0 
{\b0 \cf31 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Scope of this note
\par 
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
\u160\'3f
\par 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li0 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li0 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
This note provides an overview and commentary to the key provisions of the 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i1 \fs20 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i1 \fs20 
{\field {\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://uk.practicallaw.thomsonreuters.com/3-107-7450?originationContext=document&vr=3.0&rs=PLUK1.0&transitionType=DocumentItem&contextData=(sc.Default)" }{\fldrslt 
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i1 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Uniform Customs and Practice for Documentary Credits
}}}
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 (
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i1 \fs20 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i1 \fs20 
{\field {\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://uk.practicallaw.thomsonreuters.com/3-107-7431?originationContext=document&vr=3.0&rs=PLUK1.0&transitionType=DocumentItem&contextData=(sc.Default)" }{\fldrslt 
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i1 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
UCP
}}}
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
), 2007 Revision, ICC Publication No. 600 (
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i1 \fs20 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i1 \fs20 
{\field {\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://uk.practicallaw.thomsonreuters.com/1-107-7432?originationContext=document&vr=3.0&rs=PLUK1.0&transitionType=DocumentItem&contextData=(sc.Default)" }{\fldrslt 
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i1 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
UCP 600
}}}
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
) which superseded the prior version of the UCP, UCP 500. Where UPC 600 made particularly significant changes to the provisions of UCP 500, this note also compares the provision of UCP 600 to the comparable one contained in UCP 500. This note approaches the provisions of UCP 600 as follows:
\par 
}
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
\u160\'3f
\par 
