}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li0 {\fi-360 \li {\*\pn \pnlvlblt \ilvl0 \ls6 \pnindent0 \pnf1 {\f2 \pntxtb \u8226\'3f}}{\listtext \b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li480 \u8226\'3f\tab }\ls6 {\pntext }
{\pard }\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li480 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li480 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \ql \fs20 \li480 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa180 \sb0 
International Standard Banking Practice for the Examination of Documents under UCP 600 (ICC Banking Commission publication No. 745) (ISBP 745), which sets out what international banking practice should be when it comes to applying UCP 600.
\par {\pntext }
}
}
}
}{\fi-360 \li {\*\pn \pnlvlblt \ilvl0 \ls7 \pnindent0 \pnf1 {\f2 \pntxtb \u8226\'3f}}{\listtext \b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li480 \u8226\'3f\tab }\ls7 {\pntext }
{\pard }\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li480 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li480 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \ql \fs20 \li480 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa180 \sb0 
Uniform Rules for Bank-to-Bank Reimbursements, ICC Publication No. 725 (URR 725), and their predecessor URR 525, which provide for standard rules governing the process of bank-to-bank reimbursement.
\par {\pntext }
}
}
}
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri100 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li100 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li0 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li0 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
The UCP 600 is designed for use with documentary letters of credits (
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i1 \fs20 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i1 \fs20 
{\field {\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://uk.practicallaw.thomsonreuters.com/0-107-6758?originationContext=document&vr=3.0&rs=PLUK1.0&transitionType=DocumentItem&contextData=(sc.Default)" }{\fldrslt 
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i1 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
letters of credit
}}}
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 or credits) as distinguished from 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i1 \fs20 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i1 \fs20 
{\field {\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://uk.practicallaw.thomsonreuters.com/3-107-7308?originationContext=document&vr=3.0&rs=PLUK1.0&transitionType=DocumentItem&contextData=(sc.Default)" }{\fldrslt 
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i1 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
standby letters of credit
}}}
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 (standbys) for which the 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i1 \fs20 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i1 \fs20 
{\field {\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://uk.practicallaw.thomsonreuters.com/3-386-2985?originationContext=document&vr=3.0&rs=PLUK1.0&transitionType=DocumentItem&contextData=(sc.Default)" }{\fldrslt 
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i1 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
International Standby Practices
}}}
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
, ICC Publication No. 590 (ISP 98) were designed. Since many parties apply UCP 600 rather than ISP 98 to standby letters of credit, this note considers some of the important differences between the UCP 600 and the ISP 98 as they relate to the different functions of documentary letters of credit and standby letters of credit. For more on the differences between different types of letters of credit, see 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i1 \fs20 
{\field {\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://uk.practicallaw.thomsonreuters.com/1-107-3740?originationContext=document&vr=3.0&rs=PLUK1.0&transitionType=DocumentItem&contextData=(sc.Default)" }{\fldrslt 
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i1 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
Practice note, Letters of credit: overview
}}}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb200 
.
\par 
}
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
\u160\'3f
\par 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li0 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li0 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
This note is not a summary of the UCP 600 and should be read together with the UPC 600. The UCP 600 and related publications can be purchased from the ICC business bookstore, visit the ICC 
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i1 \fs20 
{\field {\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://uk.practicallaw.thomsonreuters.com/4-106-3396?originationContext=document&vr=3.0&rs=PLUK1.0&transitionType=DocumentItem&contextData=(sc.Default)" }{\fldrslt 
{\b0 \cf23 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i1 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
website
}}}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
 for more information. Of particular interest, the ICC have published ICC Banking Commission Opinions 2009-2011, ICC Publication No. 732. The opinions give guidance on how ICC rules are interpreted in practice by answering queries on various ICC publications, including UCP 600 and ISBP 745.
\par 
}
}
}
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ri0 \i0 \qj \fs20 \li0 
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \ul0 \strike0 \i0 \fs20 \sa0 \sb0 
\u160\'3f
}
{\b0 \cf21 \f2 \i0 \fs20 
}
